---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Terms of use" description="The terms for using this site and its content.">
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-block: 2.5rem; max-width: 47rem;">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>

    <div class="post-body">
      <p>
        Use of {site.name} is subject to the terms below. Browsing the site means accepting them.
        If you do not accept them, do not use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>What the site publishes</h2>
      <p>
        Summaries and explanations of open-source projects hosted on GitHub, written from publicly
        available repository data and other published sources. Posts are drafted with a language
        model and reviewed before publishing; the full account is on the
        <a href="/disclosure">disclosure page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>The content is not advice</h2>
      <p>
        Posts are general information. They are not professional, legal, financial or security
        advice, and they are not a substitute for evaluating a project yourself. Deciding to run,
        adopt or depend on a piece of software is your call and your risk. Verify anything that
        matters against the linked sources — and against the repository's own licence — before
        acting on it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Software moves. A post that was accurate on its publication date may be wrong two months
        later: the project may be archived, relicensed, renamed or rewritten. Every post carries
        its date, and every repository figure carries the date it was captured, for that reason.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and mistakes</h2>
      <p>
        We try to be accurate and do not guarantee it. Errors, omissions and inaccuracies are
        possible. What we find gets fixed and logged on the
        <a href="/corrections">corrections page</a>. Nothing here promises uninterrupted
        availability or a fault-free site.
      </p>

      <h2>Using our content</h2>
      <p>
        Quoting a reasonable extract for reporting, criticism or study is fine, provided the site
        is named and the original page is linked. Do not republish whole posts or substantial parts
        of them elsewhere, including in translation, and do not use them as training data for
        commercial models, without prior permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Projects, links and trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        Every post links the sources it was written from. Links are for verification and
        convenience. We do not control the content of those sites, are not responsible for it, and
        a link is not an endorsement. Project names, logos and source code belong to their owners
        and are used descriptively; each post names the licence the project carried at the time of
        writing. This site is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by GitHub, Inc. or any
        project it covers. Maintainers who want a correction, an update or a takedown can reach us
        through the <a href="/about">about page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may be updated. The version on this page is the binding one. A material change
        will also be flagged on the home page.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms and any use of the site are governed by the laws of the State of Israel, and
        the competent courts in Israel have exclusive jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms go through the <a href="/about">about page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
